#
# vivo-compatible fingerprint id node
#
menuconfig FP_ID
	bool "Legacy vivo /sys/fp_id/fp_id node"
	help
	  Provide the /sys/fp_id/fp_id character node that vivo's fingerprint
	  service (PropertiesCreator, vivo-services.jar) reads to decide which
	  fingerprint hardware is present.

	  The file contains one line of the form

	      <type>_<manufacturer>_<module>

	  where <type> is one of common / optical / udfp / ultrasonic / sidefp.

	  The first field is a keyword, NOT a number: "common" maps to
	  sensorType 1 (rear), "1" would be parsed as UNKNOWN (type 0).

	  The default content is compiled into the driver
	  (drivers/fp_id/fp_id.c, FP_ID_DEFAULT = "common_fpc_fpc1020").
	  It can be changed at runtime by writing to the node, or at boot from
	  device tree via the "vivo,fp-id" property.

	  If unsure, say N.
